Authors of predict-ng
=====================

Original Author
---------------
John A. Magliacane, KD2BD <kd2bd@amsat.org>
  Lead developer of PREDICT, the satellite tracking and orbital prediction
  program on which predict-ng is based.

Contributors to the original PREDICT
-------------------------------------
Ivan Galysh, KD4HBO <galysh@juno.nrl.navy.mil>
  Socket-based server code and the "map" client application (2000).

Vittorio Benvenuti, I3VFJ <benscosm@iol.it>
  PIC/TRACK serial port antenna rotator control code (2000).

Neoklis Kyriazis, 5B4AZ
  SGP4/SDP4 orbital models and sun/moon position algorithms (satcom-08, 2002),
  derived from FORTRAN/Pascal code by Dr. T.S. Kelso.

Xavier Crehueras, EB3CZS
  The "gsat" client application.

Rich Parry, W9IF
  Perl client demonstration program.

Steve Fraser, VK5ASF
  WinPredictClient.

Wade Hampton
  Original concept of using "xearth" as a graphical display (earthtrack).

Lapo Pieri, IK5NAX
  Squint angle calculations (trk-0.4.1).

Bent Bagger, OZ6BL
Tom Busch, WB8WOR
Takeshi Okazaki (MTSAT-1R / HIMAWARI 6)
  Code contributions.

Joeal Subash
  QuickDoppler feature.

predict-ng Maintainer
---------------------
Costin Stroie, YO3JAZ <yo3jaz@eridu.eu.org>
  Modernization: build system (configure/Makefile), kepupdate rewrite,
  SIGHUP live reload, East-positive longitude convention, elimination of
  generated predict.h, vocalizer integration, man page updates.
